  "description": "Work is done, fun begins. Meet the Rossignol After Hours T-Type e-MTB, your all-access pass to flowy trails, good times, and unforgettable sunsets.\n\nFrom smooth climbs to fluid descents, the Bosch Performance Line CX motor and our tailor-made aluminum frame deliver responsive power and an intuitive ride that keeps you in the flow. The four-bar linkage design with Fox Factory shocks offers 150 mm of travel in the back and 160 mm up front for confident control and agile handling across all terrain.\n\nThe SRAM S1000 Eagle T-Type drivetrain and powerful SRAM Maven Silver four-piston brakes with 200 mm rotors give you precise control when it matters most.\n\nClock out, and turn up the fun.\n\nUncompromising Power and Range\nDominate every ascent with the Bosch Performance Line CX motor, providing class-leading torque and fluid assistance. Paired with the high-capacity 800Wh PowerTube battery, you have the range to explore further and climb higher without ever glancing at the battery gauge\n\nIntelligent Ride Tracking\nStay connected with the Bosch Kiox 400C display. This compact, vibrant interface provides real-time ride data, navigation, and seamless integration with the Bosch ecosystem, all while staying protected on the cockpit.\n\nFactory-Level Suspension Performance\nThe Fox 38 Factory fork with the GRIPX damper sets the standard for stiffness and precision with 160 mm of travel, while the Fox Float X Factory rear shock provides 150 mm of travel to deliver elite-level traction and heat management for consistent performance on long, grueling descents\n\nT-Type Shifting\nShift with confidence with the SRAM S1000 Eagle T-Type drivetrain. Powered directly by the e-bike battery, this derailleur requires no separate charging while ensuring precise, heavy-duty shifting even under full motor assistance\n\nMassive Braking Power and Control\nSRAM Maven Silver four-piston hydraulic brakes paired with 200 mm rotors offer monumental stopping power. Specifically designed for the higher speeds and weights of modern e-MTBs, they provide the modulation and thermal management needed for total control on any terrain",
